56o|v|To take to or upon one's self; to take formally and demonstratively; sometimes, to appropriate or take unjustly. ; To take for granted, or without proof; to suppose as a fact; to suppose or take arbitrarily or tentatively. ; To pretend to possess; to take in appearance. ; To receive or adopt. ; To be arrogant or pretentious; to claim more than is due. ; To undertake, as by a promise.	o:qep,25,5;1xnz,5,5~qep,25,5;1xnz,5,5	s:16sg,49,6;1int,10,15~1int,10,15;16sg,49,6	d:1t3q,57,5;10xv,56,3;5qx,35,6;1ppo,33,3;2hq,13,7;1wdw,7,3;14yr,6,22~14yr,6,22;2hq,13,7;5qx,35,6;1t3q,57,5;1ppo,33,3;1wdw,7,3;10xv,56,3
