56x|n|The act of assuming, or taking to or upon one's self; the act of taking up or adopting. ; The act of taking for granted, or supposing a thing without proof; supposition; unwarrantable claim. ; The thing supposed; a postulate, or proposition assumed; a supposition. ; The minor or second proposition in a categorical syllogism. ; The taking of a person up into heaven. ; A festival in honor of the ascent of the Virgin Mary into heaven.	a:10xu,81,5;26yw,70,4;rjv,59,5;v4r,58,3;1ppm,41,3;2bba,39,6~2bba,39,6;10xu,81,5;rjv,59,5;26yw,70,4;1ppm,41,3;v4r,58,3	n:v4r,62,4~v4r,62,4
